sentinel::codegen::effecting_fn_body_not_direct

  × effecting fn `ls` cannot be lowered: the arguments of a `perform` or of a
  │ call to an effecting fn in it suspend themselves (a `perform`, an
  │ effecting call or a `handle`), and every body shape lowers arguments as
  │ plain values; bind a suspending argument with its own `let`, or compute a
  │ locally handled one in a separate fn
  help: an effecting fn returns a continuation, so only the shapes ADR 0072
        enumerates can be lowered; reshape the body, or wait for the wider
        seam that ADR 0072 defers
